# This repo is not built from its own Dockerfile — it reaches a build as a NAMED BuildKit context
# (`additional_contexts: sdk: <path>`), and a consumer Dockerfile does `COPY --from=sdk / ./` before
# `yarn install && yarn build`, so the WHOLE of this directory is transferred on every build.
# Without this file there was no ignore list at all: BuildKit logged `load .dockerignore`
# for this context and found nothing.
#
# Local `.claude/worktrees/<slug>` worktrees accumulate — 1.5 GB of the 1.65 GB context here on
# 2026-09-12, each carrying its own node_modules. None of it is reachable from the build: the
# image copies the context root and then installs from the lockfile.
.claude/
.worktrees/

# Build inputs only; `yarn build` (tsc -b) regenerates everything else.
.git/
.DS_Store
